rows.01:21ec:
When he spotted me, he came over, waving the flashlight in his hand.
He could at least have smiled, but he didn't crack even a hint of one.
Maybe he was nervous; his face was damp with sweat, and he just looked at me with no expression at all.{p}

rows.01:2d4c:
Yoshioka's face had looked normal in it just a moment ago, but before I knew it, the face in the mirror had turned purple.
And it wasn't a normal face, either.
How do I put it... it was swollen, or like a wax doll's face... anyway, it just wasn't normal.{p}

rows.01:2f30:
Yoshioka screaming that, and that's about it.
Even so, I never once thought about going back to help him.
Not even I wanted to go back in there again.{p}

rows.01:2fd8:
Still, I fought down my fear and waited in front of the main gate for a while.
But no matter how long I waited, he never came out.
I figured maybe he'd gone home through the back gate, so I went home too.{p}

rows.01:33a4:
I screamed, without any regard for where I was.
I couldn't help it.
There in the coffin was Yoshioka's face, the same face I'd seen reflected in that mirror.{p}

rows.01:3b00:
The mirror on the stair landing, that thing is bad news.
Listen, the story I'm about to tell you is something I really went through.
It's the story of the mirror on the old building's stairs.{p}
